>
<p data-start=3D"155" data-end=3D"425" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=3D"=
158" data-end=3D"195">protocole de communication r=C3=A9seau</strong> est u=
n ensemble de r=C3=A8gles et de conventions qui r=C3=A9gissent l'=C3=A9chan=
ge de donn=C3=A9es entre les appareils d=E2=80=99un r=C3=A9seau. Ces protoc=
oles permettent aux =C3=A9quipements de communiquer m=C3=AAme s'ils sont fa=
briqu=C3=A9s par des entreprises diff=C3=A9rentes.</p>
<p data-start=3D"427" data-end=3D"683" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"427=
" data-end=3D"461">Pourquoi sont-ils essentiels ?</strong><br data-start=3D=
"461" data-end=3D"464">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Assurent une communication standardis=C3=A9e entre les a=
ppareils.<br data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"530">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Facilitent l'interconnexion des r=C3=A9seaux =C3=A0 l'=
=C3=A9chelle mondiale (ex : Internet).<br data-start=3D"610" data-end=3D"61=
3">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Garantissent la fiabilit=C3=A9 et la s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 =
des =C3=A9changes de donn=C3=A9es.</p>
<p data-start=3D"685" data-end=3D"833" class=3D"">Dans ce chapitre, nous al=
lons examiner les principaux <strong data-start=3D"739" data-end=3D"770">pr=
otocoles de communication</strong>, class=C3=A9s selon leurs fonctions dans=
 le mod=C3=A8le OSI et TCP/IP.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"838" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"840" data-end=3D"888" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"84=
3" data-end=3D"886">2. Classification des Protocoles R=C3=A9seau</strong></=
h2>
<p data-start=3D"890" data-end=3D"1000" class=3D"">Les protocoles r=C3=A9se=
au sont g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement class=C3=A9s selon les <strong data-start=3D=
"948" data-end=3D"973">couches du mod=C3=A8le OSI</strong> et du mod=C3=A8l=
e <strong data-start=3D"987" data-end=3D"997">TCP/IP</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1002" data-end=3D"1033" class=3D"">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1005" data-end=3D"1031">Mod=C3=A8le OSI (7 couches)</strong></p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"1034" data-end=3D"1271">
<li data-start=3D"1034" data-end=3D"1073" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1036" data-end=3D"1073" class=3D"">Application (HTTP, FTP,=
 SMTP, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1074" data-end=3D"1107" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1076" data-end=3D"1107" class=3D"">Pr=C3=A9sentation (SSL/=
TLS, ASCII)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1108" data-end=3D"1131" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1110" data-end=3D"1131" class=3D"">Session (RPC, PPTP)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1132" data-end=3D"1156" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1134" data-end=3D"1156" class=3D"">Transport (TCP, UDP)</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1157" data-end=3D"1183" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1159" data-end=3D"1183" class=3D"">R=C3=A9seau (IP, ICMP, =
ARP)</p>
