<h2 data-start=3D"48" data-end=3D"95" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"51" =
data-end=3D"95">Chapitre : Routage Statique et Dynamique</strong></h2>
<hr data-start=3D"97" data-end=3D"100" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"102" data-end=3D"135" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"10=
5" data-end=3D"135">1. Introduction au Routage</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"136" data-end=3D"436" class=3D"">Le routage est le process=
us qui permet d=E2=80=99acheminer des paquets de donn=C3=A9es entre des r=
=C3=A9seaux distincts en utilisant des =C3=A9quipements appel=C3=A9s <stron=
g data-start=3D"275" data-end=3D"287">routeurs</strong>. Un routeur utilise=
 une <strong data-start=3D"312" data-end=3D"332">table de routage</strong> =
pour stocker les informations sur les chemins disponibles afin de prendre d=
es d=C3=A9cisions d=E2=80=99acheminement.</p>
<p data-start=3D"438" data-end=3D"486" class=3D"">Il existe deux principale=
s m=C3=A9thodes de routage :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"487" data-end=3D"675">
<li data-start=3D"487" data-end=3D"571" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"490" data-end=3D"571" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"490=
" data-end=3D"510">Routage statique</strong> : l=E2=80=99administrateur r=
=C3=A9seau configure manuellement les routes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"572" data-end=3D"675" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"575" data-end=3D"675" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"575=
" data-end=3D"596">Routage dynamique</strong> : le routeur apprend automati=
quement les routes via des protocoles de routage.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"677" data-end=3D"765" class=3D"">Chaque m=C3=A9thode a ses=
 avantages et ses inconv=C3=A9nients, que nous allons examiner en d=C3=A9ta=
il.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"767" data-end=3D"770" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"772" data-end=3D"798" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"77=
5" data-end=3D"798">2. Routage Statique</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"799" data-end=3D"822" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"80=
3" data-end=3D"822">2.1. D=C3=A9finition</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"823" data-end=3D"1040" class=3D"">Le routage statique cons=
iste =C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"854" data-end=3D"889">ajouter manuellemen=
t des routes</strong> dans la table de routage. Ce type de routage est simp=
le, mais peu =C3=A9volutif, car il n=C3=A9cessite une intervention humaine =
=C3=A0 chaque modification du r=C3=A9seau.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1042" data-end=3D"1081" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1046" data-end=3D"1081">2.2. Avantages et Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"108=
