<hr data-start=3D"2508" data-end=3D"2511" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2513" data-end=3D"2540" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2516" data-end=3D"2540">3. Routage Dynamique</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2541" data-end=3D"2564" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2545" data-end=3D"2564">3.1. D=C3=A9finition</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2565" data-end=3D"2848" class=3D"">Le routage dynamique pe=
rmet aux routeurs d'=C3=A9changer des informations sur les r=C3=A9seaux acc=
essibles en utilisant des <strong data-start=3D"2679" data-end=3D"2714">pro=
tocoles de routage dynamique</strong>. Ces protocoles permettent au routeur=
 de <strong data-start=3D"2756" data-end=3D"2809">mettre =C3=A0 jour automa=
tiquement sa table de routage</strong> en fonction des changements du r=C3=
=A9seau.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2850" data-end=3D"2889" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2854" data-end=3D"2889">3.2. Avantages et Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"289=
0" data-end=3D"3250" node=3D"[object Object]"><thead data-start=3D"2890" da=
ta-end=3D"2927"><tr data-start=3D"2890" data-end=3D"2927"><th data-start=3D=
"2890" data-end=3D"2906"><strong data-start=3D"2892" data-end=3D"2905">Avan=
tages</strong></th><th data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"2927"><strong data-s=
tart=3D"2908" data-end=3D"2925">Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong></th></tr></thea=
d><tbody data-start=3D"2962" data-end=3D"3250"><tr data-start=3D"2962" data=
-end=3D"3041"><td>Mise =C3=A0 jour automatique des routes</td><td>Consomme =
des ressources CPU et m=C3=A9moire</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"3042" data-en=
d=3D"3160"><td>R=C3=A9agit aux changements du r=C3=A9seau (convergence auto=
matique)</td><td>Risque d=E2=80=99instabilit=C3=A9 en cas de mauvaise confi=
guration</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"3161" data-end=3D"3250"><td>R=C3=A9duit=
 le risque d'erreur humaine</td><td>Plus complexe =C3=A0 configurer qu=E2=
=80=99un routage statique</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3 data-start=3D"3252" data-end=3D"3305" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3256" data-end=3D"3305">3.3. Types de Protocoles de Routage Dynamique</stro=
ng></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3306" data-end=3D"3375" class=3D"">Les protocoles de routa=
ge dynamique sont class=C3=A9s en deux cat=C3=A9gories :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"3377" data-end=3D"3436" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3382" data-end=3D"3436">3.3.1. Protocoles de Routage =C3=A0 Vecteur de Dist=
ance</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3437" data-end=3D"3564" class=3D"">Ces protocoles utilisen=
t le <strong data-start=3D"3465" data-end=3D"3484">nombre de sauts</strong>=
 (hops) comme crit=C3=A8re principal pour d=C3=A9terminer le meilleur chemi=
n.<br data-start=3D"3551" data-end=3D"3554">
Exemples :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3565" data-end=3D"3662">
<li data-start=3D"3565" data-end=3D"3605" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3567" data-end=3D"3605" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
567" data-end=3D"3605">RIP (Routing Information Protocol)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3606" data-end=3D"3662" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3608" data-end=3D"3662" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
608" data-end=3D"3662">EIGRP (Enhanced Interior Gateway Routing Protocol)</=
strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3664" data-end=3D"3716" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3669" data-end=3D"3716">3.3.2. Protocoles de Routage =C3=A0 =C3=89tat de Li=
en</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3717" data-end=3D"3848" class=3D"">Ces protocoles cr=C3=A9=
ent une <strong data-start=3D"3743" data-end=3D"3771">carte compl=C3=A8te d=
u r=C3=A9seau</strong> et calculent le meilleur chemin =C3=A0 l'aide d'algo=
rithmes avanc=C3=A9s.<br data-start=3D"3835" data-end=3D"3838">
Exemples :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3849" data-end=3D"3943">
<li data-start=3D"3849" data-end=3D"3886" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3851" data-end=3D"3886" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
851" data-end=3D"3886">OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3887" data-end=3D"3943" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3889" data-end=3D"3943" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
889" data-end=3D"3943">IS-IS (Intermediate System to Intermediate System)</=
strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3945" data-end=3D"3992" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3950" data-end=3D"3992">3.3.3. Protocoles de Routage Ext=C3=A9rieur</strong=
></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3993" data-end=3D"4060" class=3D"">Utilis=C3=A9s pour l'in=
terconnexion de r=C3=A9seaux sur Internet.<br data-start=3D"4048" data-end=
=3D"4051">
Exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4061" data-end=3D"4096">
<li data-start=3D"4061" data-end=3D"4096" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4063" data-end=3D"4096" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
063" data-end=3D"4096">BGP (Border Gateway Protocol)</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4098" data-end=3D"4101" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4103" data-end=3D"4172" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4106" data-end=3D"4172">4. Configuration des Protocoles de Routage Dynamiqu=
e sur Cisco</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4173" data-end=3D"4237" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4177" data-end=3D"4237">4.1. Configuration de RIP (Routing Information Prot=
ocol)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4238" data-end=3D"4339" class=3D"">RIP est un protocole si=
mple bas=C3=A9 sur la <strong data-start=3D"4278" data-end=3D"4308">distanc=
e (nombre de sauts)</strong>. Il est limit=C3=A9 =C3=A0 <strong data-start=
=3D"4326" data-end=3D"4338">15 sauts</strong>.</p>
