<p data-start=3D"154" data-end=3D"526" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D"=
157" data-end=3D"178">routage dynamique</strong> est une m=C3=A9thode perme=
ttant aux routeurs de <strong data-start=3D"222" data-end=3D"277">mettre =
=C3=A0 jour automatiquement leur table de routage</strong> en fonction des =
modifications du r=C3=A9seau. Contrairement au routage statique, o=C3=B9 le=
s routes sont d=C3=A9finies manuellement, les protocoles de routage dynamiq=
ue =C3=A9changent en permanence des informations pour optimiser les chemins=
 emprunt=C3=A9s par les paquets.</p>
<p data-start=3D"528" data-end=3D"613" class=3D"">Les principaux protocoles=
 de routage dynamique utilis=C3=A9s dans les r=C3=A9seaux Cisco sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"749">
<li data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"654" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"616" data-end=3D"654" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"616=
" data-end=3D"654">RIP (Routing Information Protocol)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"655" data-end=3D"692" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"657" data-end=3D"692" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"657=
" data-end=3D"692">OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"693" data-end=3D"749" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"695" data-end=3D"749" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"695=
" data-end=3D"749">EIGRP (Enhanced Interior Gateway Routing Protocol)</stro=
ng></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"806" class=3D"">Ces protocoles se classen=
t en deux grandes cat=C3=A9gories :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"807" data-end=3D"1096">
<li data-start=3D"807" data-end=3D"959" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"809" data-end=3D"959" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"809=
" data-end=3D"845">Protocoles =C3=A0 vecteur de distance</strong> (RIP, EIG=
RP) : Choisissent le meilleur chemin en fonction de la distance (nombre de =
sauts, bande passante, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"960" data-end=3D"1096" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"962" data-end=3D"1096" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"96=
2" data-end=3D"991">Protocoles =C3=A0 =C3=A9tat de lien</strong> (OSPF) : C=
onstruisent une carte compl=C3=A8te du r=C3=A9seau et utilisent des algorit=
hmes avanc=C3=A9s pour le routage.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1098" data-end=3D"1210" class=3D"">Nous allons explorer ch=
aque protocole en d=C3=A9tail, leur fonctionnement et leur configuration su=
r un routeur Cisco.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1212" data-end=3D"1215" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1217" data-end=3D"1261" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1220" data-end=3D"1261">2. RIP (Routing Information Protocol)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1262" data-end=3D"1294" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1266" data-end=3D"1294">2.1. Pr=C3=A9sentation de RIP</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1479" class=3D"">RIP est l=E2=80=99un de=
s plus anciens protocoles de routage dynamique. Il est bas=C3=A9 sur <stron=
g data-start=3D"1374" data-end=3D"1406">l=E2=80=99algorithme de Bellman-For=
d</strong> et utilise le <strong data-start=3D"1421" data-end=3D"1452">nomb=
re de sauts (hop count)</strong> comme m=C3=A9trique principale.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1481" data-end=3D"1517" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1485" data-end=3D"1517">2.2. Caract=C3=A9ristiques de RIP</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1518" data-end=3D"1948">
<li data-start=3D"1518" data-end=3D"1553" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1553" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
520" data-end=3D"1547">Distance administrative</strong> : 120</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1554" data-end=3D"1653" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1556" data-end=3D"1653" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
556" data-end=3D"1568">M=C3=A9trique</strong> : Nombre de sauts (limit=C3=
=A9 =C3=A0 15, au-del=C3=A0 le r=C3=A9seau est consid=C3=A9r=C3=A9 comme in=
atteignable)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1654" data-end=3D"1699" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1656" data-end=3D"1699" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
656" data-end=3D"1677">Type de protocole</strong> : Vecteur de distance</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1700" data-end=3D"1793" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1702" data-end=3D"1793" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
702" data-end=3D"1718">Mises =C3=A0 jour</strong> : Envoy=C3=A9es toutes le=
s 30 secondes (ce qui peut entra=C3=AEner de la congestion)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1794" data-end=3D"1948" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1796" data-end=3D"1810" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
796" data-end=3D"1808">Versions</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1813" data-end=3D"1948">
<li data-start=3D"1813" data-end=3D"1871" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1815" data-end=3D"1871" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
815" data-end=3D"1825">RIP v1</strong> : Ne supporte pas les sous-r=C3=A9se=
aux (classful)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1874" data-end=3D"1948" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1876" data-end=3D"1948" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
876" data-end=3D"1886">RIP v2</strong> : Supporte les sous-r=C3=A9seaux (cl=
assless) et l=E2=80=99authentification</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1950" data-end=3D"2004" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1954" data-end=3D"2004">2.3. Configuration de RIP sur un Routeur Cisco</str=
