<h2 data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2578" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2540" data-end=3D"2578">3. OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2579" data-end=3D"2612" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2583" data-end=3D"2612">3.1. Pr=C3=A9sentation de OSPF</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2613" data-end=3D"2881" class=3D"">OSPF est un protocole d=
e routage =C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"2648" data-end=3D"2664">=C3=A9tat de=
 lien</strong> qui utilise l=E2=80=99<strong data-start=3D"2679" data-end=
=3D"2705">algorithme de Dijkstra</strong> pour calculer le chemin le plus c=
ourt. Contrairement =C3=A0 RIP, il ne se base pas uniquement sur le nombre =
de sauts, mais prend en compte des <strong data-start=3D"2844" data-end=3D"=
2880">facteurs comme la bande passante</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2883" data-end=3D"2920" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2887" data-end=3D"2920">3.2. Caract=C3=A9ristiques de OSPF</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2921" data-end=3D"3154">
<li data-start=3D"2921" data-end=3D"2956" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2923" data-end=3D"2956" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
923" data-end=3D"2950">Distance administrative</strong> : 110</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2957" data-end=3D"3012" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2959" data-end=3D"3012" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
959" data-end=3D"2971">M=C3=A9trique</strong> : Co=C3=BBt (calcul=C3=A9 sel=
on la bande passante)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3013" data-end=3D"3051" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3015" data-end=3D"3051" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
015" data-end=3D"3036">Type de protocole</strong> : =C3=89tat de lien</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3052" data-end=3D"3154" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3054" data-end=3D"3154" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
054" data-end=3D"3079">Organisation en aires</strong> : N=C3=A9cessite une =
structure hi=C3=A9rarchique avec une <strong data-start=3D"3128" data-end=
=3D"3154">aire backbone (area 0)</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
