<h4 data-start=3D"2574" data-end=3D"2622" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2579" data-end=3D"2622">1.1.4. V=C3=A9rification et D=C3=A9pannage d=E2=80=
=99OSPF</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2623" data-end=3D"2721" class=3D"">Pour v=C3=A9rifier les =
informations de zone et la connectivit=C3=A9 OSPF, utilisez les commandes s=
uivantes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2722" data-end=3D"2998">
<li data-start=3D"2722" data-end=3D"2782" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2724" data-end=3D"2782" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"272=
4" data-end=3D"2747">show ip ospf neighbor</code> : Affiche l'=C3=A9tat des=
 voisins OSPF.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2783" data-end=3D"2857" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2785" data-end=3D"2857" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"278=
5" data-end=3D"2809">show ip ospf interface</code> : Affiche les interfaces=
 configur=C3=A9es pour OSPF.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2858" data-end=3D"2935" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2860" data-end=3D"2935" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"286=
0" data-end=3D"2883">show ip ospf database</code> : Affiche la base de donn=
=C3=A9es de lien d'=C3=A9tat (LSDB).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2936" data-end=3D"2998" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2938" data-end=3D"2998" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"293=
8" data-end=3D"2958">show ip route ospf</code> : Affiche les routes apprise=
s via OSPF.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3000" data-end=3D"3003" class=3D"">
<h3 data-start=3D"3005" data-end=3D"3063" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3009" data-end=3D"3063">1.2. OSPF et VLSM (Variable Length Subnet Masking)<=
/strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3065" data-end=3D"3288" class=3D"">OSPF prend en charge le=
 VLSM, ce qui permet de cr=C3=A9er des sous-r=C3=A9seaux de tailles vari=C3=
=A9es sur un m=C3=AAme r=C3=A9seau. Cependant, il y a des r=C3=A8gles conce=
rnant la gestion des sous-r=C3=A9seaux avec diff=C3=A9rentes tailles de mas=
que dans OSPF :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"3290" data-end=3D"3343" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3295" data-end=3D"3343">1.2.1. Configurer des sous-r=C3=A9seaux avec VLSM</=
strong></h4>
<ol data-start=3D"3344" data-end=3D"3733">
<li data-start=3D"3344" data-end=3D"3733" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3347" data-end=3D"3528" class=3D"">Pour configurer un r=C3=
=A9seau avec plusieurs sous-r=C3=A9seaux sur OSPF, vous devez inclure les r=
