<h2 data-start=3D"73" data-end=3D"145" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"76"=
 data-end=3D"145">Concepts de SDN et Cisco ACI (Application Centric Infrast=
ructure)</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"147" data-end=3D"569" class=3D"">Dans le cadre de la certi=
fication <strong data-start=3D"181" data-end=3D"195">Cisco CCNP</strong>, l=
a compr=C3=A9hension de la <strong data-start=3D"220" data-end=3D"250">virt=
ualisation des r=C3=A9seaux</strong> et du <strong data-start=3D"257" data-=
end=3D"294">Software Defined Networking (SDN)</strong> est essentielle pour=
 ma=C3=AEtriser les techniques modernes de gestion des r=C3=A9seaux. En par=
ticulier, la <strong data-start=3D"393" data-end=3D"443">Cisco ACI (Applica=
tion Centric Infrastructure)</strong> constitue une solution SDN sp=C3=A9ci=
fique de Cisco, con=C3=A7ue pour r=C3=A9pondre aux exigences complexes des =
