trong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6117" data-end=3D"6153" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6121" data-end=3D"6153">4.1. Planification de l'IPv6</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6155" data-end=3D"6332" class=3D"">L'IPv6 est l'avenir de =
l'adressage IP, surtout face =C3=A0 l'=C3=A9puisement des adresses IPv4. Le=
s adresses IPv6 sont =C3=A9crites sur 128 bits, offrant ainsi une capacit=
=C3=A9 d'adressage =C3=A9norme.</p>
<ol data-start=3D"6334" data-end=3D"6737">
<li data-start=3D"6334" data-end=3D"6537" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6337" data-end=3D"6365" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
337" data-end=3D"6363">Plages d'adresses IPv6</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6369" data-end=3D"6537">
<li data-start=3D"6369" data-end=3D"6444" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6371" data-end=3D"6444" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
371" data-end=3D"6389">Plage publique</strong> : Les adresses commencent g=
=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement par <code data-start=3D"6433" data-end=3D"6443">2000:=
:/3</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6448" data-end=3D"6537" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6450" data-end=3D"6537" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
450" data-end=3D"6495">Plage priv=C3=A9e (Unique Local Address - ULA)</stro=
ng> : Les adresses commencent par <code data-start=3D"6526" data-end=3D"653=
6">FC00::/7</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6539" data-end=3D"6737" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6542" data-end=3D"6737" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
542" data-end=3D"6579">Utilisation des sous-r=C3=A9seaux IPv6</strong> :
L'IPv6 permet de sous-r=C3=A9seauter de mani=C3=A8re plus flexible. Chaque =
sous-r=C3=A9seau est g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement de <code data-start=3D"6682" da=
ta-end=3D"6687">/64</code>, offrant une plage de 18 quintillions d'adresses=
.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h4 data-start=3D"6739" data-end=3D"6788" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6744" data-end=3D"6786">Exemple de calcul de sous-r=C3=A9seaux IPv6</strong=
> :</h4>
<p data-start=3D"6789" data-end=3D"6989" class=3D"">Si vous avez une adress=
e IPv6 <code data-start=3D"6819" data-end=3D"6845">2001:0db8:85a3:0000::/64=
</code>, vous pouvez cr=C3=A9er des sous-r=C3=A9seaux en utilisant la notat=
ion <code data-start=3D"6907" data-end=3D"6913">/128</code> pour des h=C3=
=B4tes individuels ou <code data-start=3D"6944" data-end=3D"6950">/120</cod=
e> pour des sous-r=C3=A9seaux suppl=C3=A9mentaires.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6991" data-end=3D"6994" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6996" data-end=3D"7057" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
