<hr data-start=3D"5423" data-end=3D"5426" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5428" data-end=3D"5467" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5431" data-end=3D"5467">4. BGP (Border Gateway Protocol)</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5469" data-end=3D"5506" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5473" data-end=3D"5506">4.1. Pr=C3=A9sentation et Objectif</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5507" data-end=3D"5784" class=3D"">BGP est un protocole de=
 routage inter-domaine (EGP) utilis=C3=A9 principalement pour le routage en=
tre diff=C3=A9rents syst=C3=A8mes autonomes (AS). BGP est essentiel pour l'=
Internet car il permet de d=C3=A9finir comment les donn=C3=A9es circulent e=
ntre diff=C3=A9rents fournisseurs d'acc=C3=A8s =C3=A0 Internet (FAI).</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"5786" data-end=3D"5811" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5791" data-end=3D"5811">Avantages de BGP</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"5812" data-end=3D"6096">
<li data-start=3D"5812" data-end=3D"5939" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5814" data-end=3D"5939" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
814" data-end=3D"5844">Scalabilit=C3=A9 et flexibilit=C3=A9</strong> : BGP =
peut g=C3=A9rer un tr=C3=A8s grand nombre de routes, ce qui le rend adapt=
=C3=A9 pour l'Internet global.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5940" data-end=3D"6096" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5942" data-end=3D"6096" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
942" data-end=3D"5972">Contr=C3=B4le pr=C3=A9cis du routage</strong> : BGP =
permet de manipuler les chemins en fonction de crit=C3=A8res comme les pr=
=C3=A9fixes, les AS Path et les politiques de routage.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"6098" data-end=3D"6121" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6103" data-end=3D"6121">Limites de BGP</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"6122" data-end=3D"6372">
<li data-start=3D"6122" data-end=3D"6215" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6124" data-end=3D"6215" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
124" data-end=3D"6145">Convergence lente</strong> : BGP prend plus de temps=
 pour converger par rapport =C3=A0 OSPF ou EIGRP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6216" data-end=3D"6372" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6218" data-end=3D"6372" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
218" data-end=3D"6249">Complexit=C3=A9 de configuration</strong> : La confi=
guration de BGP peut =C3=AAtre complexe, notamment en raison de la n=C3=A9c=
essit=C3=A9 de g=C3=A9rer plusieurs crit=C3=A8res de filtrage.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6374" data-end=3D"6408" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6378" data-end=3D"6408">4.2. Fonctionnement de BGP</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6409" data-end=3D"6565" class=3D"">BGP est un protocole de=
 routage bas=C3=A9 sur les chemins, c'est-=C3=A0-dire qu'il choisit les rou=
tes en fonction des chemins AS plut=C3=B4t qu'en fonction de la distance.</=
p>
<ul data-start=3D"6566" data-end=3D"7004">
<li data-start=3D"6566" data-end=3D"6694" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6568" data-end=3D"6694" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
568" data-end=3D"6579">AS Path</strong> : Chaque route BGP contient un enre=
gistrement des AS travers=C3=A9s. Cela permet =C3=A0 BGP d'=C3=A9viter les =
boucles de routage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6695" data-end=3D"6877" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6697" data-end=3D"6877" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
697" data-end=3D"6711">Attributes</strong> : BGP utilise plusieurs attribut=
s pour influencer le choix de la route, comme <strong data-start=3D"6790" d=
ata-end=3D"6800">Weight</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"6802" data-end=3D"6=
822">Local Preference</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"6824" data-end=3D"683=
5">AS Path</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"6837" data-end=3D"6871">MED (Mul=
ti-Exit Discriminator)</strong>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6878" data-end=3D"7004" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6880" data-end=3D"7004" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
880" data-end=3D"6896">Peerings BGP</strong> : Les routeurs BGP =C3=A9tabli=
ssent des sessions de pairage entre eux pour =C3=A9changer des informations=
 de routage.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7006" data-end=3D"7047" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7010" data-end=3D"7047">4.3. Configuration de base de BGP</strong></h3>
